          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 7.4: Let us observe and calculate"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.126,
            0.743,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us now try to find the smallest value that a given laboratory thermometer can read."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.173,
            0.743,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Again, take the same laboratory thermometer which you used in Activity 7.3 and observe it carefully."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.219,
            0.43,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note down the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.245,
            0.743,
            0.288
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How much is the temperature difference indicated between the two bigger marks?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.291,
            0.743,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "— How many divisions (shown by smaller marks) are there between these two bigger marks?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.358,
            0.743,
            0.4
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How much temperature does one small division indicate?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.405,
            0.743,
            0.446
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the smallest value that the thermometer can read is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.452,
            0.744,
            0.513
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 7.3b shows a closeup of a part of the thermometer shown in Fig. 7.3a. Can you now find the smallest value that this thermometer can read?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.516,
            0.16,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.119,
                0.516,
                0.16,
                0.802
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_8_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.514,
            0.744,
            0.616
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For the thermometer shown in Fig. 7.3b, the temperature difference indicated between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 0 ~ ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or between "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10 \\;  °C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "20\\ ^{\\circ} C"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\tt 1 0 ~ ^ { \\circ } C } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " And the number of divisions between these marks are 10 divisions. So, one small division can read "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "10/10=1^{\\circ}C."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.616,
            0.743,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "That is, the smallest value that this thermometer can read is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1   ^ { \\circ } \\mathbb { C } ,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.656,
            0.744,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Your school laboratory may have thermometers for which the range and the value of the smallest division may be different. It is, therefore, always necessary to look carefully at the thermometer you are about to use."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.216,
            0.758,
            0.744,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You have learnt how to find the temperature range of a given laboratory thermometer. You have also learnt how to find the smallest value that a given laboratory thermometer can read. We will now learn how to measure temperature using a laboratory thermometer. But, let us first learn how to use a laboratory thermometer correctly."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.808,
            0.222,
            0.91
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 7.3(b): Closeup of a part of the thermometer shown in Fig. 7.3a."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.866,
            0.69,
            0.885,
            0.86
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Temperature and its Measurement"
